.TH DEV 1 "2026-07-11" "dev @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dev \- on-device voice and Apple Intelligence from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dev
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ prompt ]
.br
.B dev
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-
.I prompt
.br
.B dev
.B \-f
.I file
.RI [ options ]
.I prompt
.br
.B dev
.B \-\-chat
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B dev
.B \-\-stream
.RI [ options ]
.I prompt
.br
.B dev
.B \-\-serve
.RI [ server-options ]
.br
.B dev
.B \-\-benchmark
.br
.B dev
.B \-\-count-tokens
.RI [ options ]
.I prompt
.br
.B dev
.B \-\-model-info
.br
.B dev
.B \-\-update
.br
.B dev
.B \-\-demos
.RI [ dir ]
.br
.B dev
.B \-\-speak
.RI [ text ]
.br
.B dev
.B \-\-listen
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B dev
.B \-\-agent
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B dev
.B completions
.I shell
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dev
is a command-line interface and OpenAI-compatible HTTP server for
Apple's on-device FoundationModels large language model, extended with
native text-to-speech and speech-to-text. Inference runs entirely
on-device on Apple Silicon Macs that have Apple Intelligence enabled
(for LLM modes). No data leaves the machine for inference.
.PP
.B dev
has six modes:
.TP
.B unix tool
Send a single prompt from arguments or standard input and receive
the response on standard output. Pipe-friendly. Respects
.BR NO_COLOR (7),
isatty detection, and returns structured exit codes for scripting.
.TP
.B interactive chat
Run an interactive multi-turn conversation with readline editing,
history, and automatic context trimming.
.TP
.B HTTP server
Expose an OpenAI-compatible HTTP API on a loopback or public port,
suitable as a drop-in replacement for code written against
.I openai.OpenAI(base_url=...) .
Includes
.BR /v1/audio/speech ", "
.BR /v1/audio/transcriptions ", and "
.BR /v1/audio/voices .
.TP
.B text-to-speech
With
.BR \-\-speak ", read text from an argument or standard input and speak"
it through the default output device. Does not require Apple
Intelligence.
.TP
.B speech-to-text
With
.BR \-\-listen ", capture audio from the default microphone and print"
the transcript on standard output. Requires Microphone and Speech
Recognition permissions.
.TP
.B voice agent
With
.BR \-\-agent ", run a loop: listen from the microphone, send the"
transcript to the on-device model, and speak the answer. Press
Ctrl-C to quit. Requires Apple Intelligence and speech permissions.
.PP
The model's context window is approximately 4096 tokens. Requests
that exceed it are trimmed according to the active context strategy
or rejected with exit code 4 if the
.B strict
strategy is selected.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options. Everything after
.B \-\-
is taken as the prompt verbatim, even if it starts with a dash.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " " \fIpath\fR
Attach file content to the prompt. Repeatable; accepts multiple
files.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-system " " \fItext\fR
Set a system prompt. Applied once per session.
.TP
.BI \-\-system-file " path"
Read the system prompt from a file.
.TP
.BI \-\-schema " path"
Constrain the response to the JSON Schema in
.IR path .
The model output is guaranteed to be a single schema-valid JSON object,
printed to stdout (ideal for piping into
.BR jq ).
Single-prompt mode only: cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-chat ,
.BR \-\-stream ,
or MCP tool calling, and the schema is always read from a file, never
from stdin. A malformed or unsupported schema is a usage error (exit 2).
Supported schema subset: object, string (with enum), integer, number,
boolean, and array.
.TP
.BI \-\-messages " path"
One-shot multi-turn: read an OpenAI-style conversation (a JSON array of
message objects, or an object with a
.B messages
key) from
.I path
and print the next assistant message. Pass
.B \-
to read the conversation from piped stdin. Roles
.BR system ,
.BR user ,
.BR assistant ,
and
.B tool
are honored; the last message must be a
.B user
or
.B tool
turn (same rule as the HTTP server). Composes with
.B \-\-stream
and
.BR \-\-schema ;
cannot be combined with a positional prompt,
.BR \-f ,
or
.BR \-\-chat .
A malformed conversation is a usage error (exit 2).
.TP
.B \-\-code
Print only the code: crop the response to the content of its first
fenced code block, with the fence markers and any surrounding prose
removed. A steering directive is appended to the system prompt so the
model answers with exactly one fenced block; the crop is applied
deterministically regardless. When the response contains no fence at
all, the whole response is passed through as the code (a fully steered
model omits the fence), and a response that is exactly one inline
code span is unwrapped. Output is newline-terminated. An empty
response writes nothing and exits
.BR 7 .
Composes with
.BR \-s ,
.BR \-f ,
.BR \-\-messages ,
and piped stdin; with
.B \-\-output json
the envelope carries the cropped code as
.B content
plus an advisory
.B language
key. Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-stream ,
.BR \-\-chat ,
or
.BR \-\-schema .
The crop shapes the format, not the correctness, of the answer.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIformat\fR
Output format.
.I format
is
.B plain
(default) or
.BR json .
In
.B json
mode, a single JSON object with
.BR content ,
.BR usage ,
and
.B finish_reason
keys is written to stdout.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non-essential output such as banners and chat headers.
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable ANSI color output. Equivalent to setting
.BR NO_COLOR .
.TP
.BI \-\-temperature " n"
Sampling temperature. Non-negative float, e.g.
.BR 0.7 .
A value of
.B 0
gives deterministic (greedy) output.
.TP
.BI \-\-top-p " n"
Nucleus (top-p) sampling threshold. Float in
.BR "(0, 1]" ,
e.g.
.BR 0.9 .
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " n"
Random seed for reproducible output. Positive integer.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-tokens " n"
Maximum number of tokens to generate in the response.
.TP
.BI \-\-mcp " path|url"
Attach a local or remote Model Context Protocol tool server.
Repeatable; attach multiple servers by repeating the flag. Local
servers are stdio subprocesses; remote servers are HTTP endpoints.
.TP
.BI \-\-mcp-token " token"
Bearer token for authenticating to a remote MCP server. Prefer the
.B DEV_MCP_TOKEN
environment variable so the token does not appear in process lists.
.TP
.BI \-\-mcp-timeout " n"
MCP server timeout in seconds. Default
.BR 5 .
.TP
.B \-\-permissive
Use permissive content guardrails for the session. The default
guardrail profile enforces Apple's standard safety policies.
.TP
.BR \-\-retry " [" \fIn\fR ]
Enable retry with exponential backoff on transient errors. Defaults
to
.B 3
retries when the flag is given without a value. The optional count is
ambiguous with a numeric prompt: when a number is the only token left
.RB ( "dev \-\-retry 7" )
it is kept as the prompt with the default count, and the number is
consumed as the count only when a further token follows it
.RB ( "dev \-\-retry 3 \[dq]prompt\[dq]" ).
Use
.BI \-\-retry= n
for the unambiguous spelling.
.TP
.B \-\-model-info
Print the active model's capabilities and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-benchmark
Run the internal performance benchmark suite.
.TP
.B \-\-count-tokens
Count tokens for the given prompt without calling the model.
Accepts the same input flags as a single prompt
.RB ( \-f ,
.BR \-\-system ,
.BR \-\-mcp ,
etc.).
Counts use the on-device tokenizer API (macOS 26.4+).
When that API is unusable (older macOS, or Apple Intelligence unavailable),
counts fall back to a chars/4 approximation: a warning naming the reason is
printed to standard error, and JSON output
.RB ( \-o " json" )
carries an
.B approximate
field set to true.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
With
.BR \-\-count-tokens ,
exit with status
.B 4
if the input exceeds the token budget.
.TP
.B \-\-update
Check for updates and, if available, upgrade via Homebrew.
.TP
.B \-\-demos\fR \fI[dir]\fR
Write the bundled demo scripts to
.I dir
(default
.BR ./dev-demos ).
The demos are embedded in the binary, so this works the same regardless of how dev was installed.
.TP
.B completions \fIshell\fR
Print a shell completion script to standard output.
.I shell
is one of
.BR bash ", " zsh ", or " fish .
Completion covers all flags, the five context strategies for
.BR \-\-context-strategy ,
and file completion for
.BR \-f .
This is a subcommand, not an option; it exits after printing.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable verbose debug logging to standard error in every mode.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-release
Print detailed release and build information and exit.
.SH "VOICE OPTIONS"
Voice options apply to
.BR \-\-speak ", "
.BR \-\-listen ", "
.BR \-\-agent ", and the "
.BR /v1/audio/* "
server routes.
.TP
.BI \-\-speak " [text]"
Speak
.I text
through the default output device. When
.I text
is omitted, read from standard input. Does not call the LLM.
.TP
.B \-\-listen
Capture speech from the default microphone and print the transcript
on standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-agent
Run a voice Q&A loop: listen, ask the on-device model, speak the
answer. Press Ctrl-C to quit.
.TP
.BI \-\-input-device " uid"
Microphone device UID. When omitted, the system default input is used.
.TP
.BI \-\-voice-name " id"
TTS voice identifier, a BCP-47 language tag, or
.B personal
for Personal Voice. Default: system voice for the active locale.
.TP
.BI \-\-locale " id"
Speech recognition locale (e.g.
.BR en-US ).
.TP
.BI \-\-rate " n"
Speaking rate from
.B 0.25
to
.BR 4.0 .
.TP
.BI \-\-audio-format " fmt"
File format for server TTS rendering:
.BR wav " (default), "
.BR pcm ", or "
.BR aac .
.B mp3
and
.B opus
are not supported on-device.
.TP
.B \-\-timestamps
Include timing segments in transcription responses
.RB ( verbose_json ", " srt ", " vtt ).
.SH "CONTEXT OPTIONS"
.TP
.BI \-\-context-strategy " strategy"
Context-management strategy applied when the conversation approaches
the model's context window. One of
.BR newest-first " (default), "
.BR oldest-first ", "
.BR sliding-window ", "
.BR summarize ", or "
.BR strict
(error on overflow with exit code 4).
.TP
.BI \-\-context-max-turns " n"
Maximum number of history turns to retain. Only meaningful with
.BR sliding-window .
.TP
.BI \-\-context-output-reserve " n"
Tokens reserved for the model's output. Default
.BR 512 .
.TP
.B \-\-context-status
Print the current chat context fill after each turn.
.SH "SERVER OPTIONS"
.TP
.B \-\-serve
Start the OpenAI-compatible HTTP server.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " number"
Port to bind. Default
.BR 11434 .
.TP
.BI \-\-host " address"
Bind address. Default
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
Use
.B 0.0.0.0
to accept connections on all interfaces.
.TP
.B \-\-cors
Emit permissive CORS headers for browser clients.
.TP
.BI \-\-allowed-origins " origins"
Comma-separated list of additional origins to permit alongside the
localhost defaults.
.TP
.B \-\-no-origin-check
Disable the origin check entirely. Allows any origin. Dangerous on
non-loopback binds.
.TP
.BI \-\-token " secret"
Require a
.B Bearer
token on all requests except
.B /health
(see
.BR \-\-public-health ).
.TP
.B \-\-token-auto
Generate a random Bearer token, require it, and print it to stderr
once at startup.
.TP
.B \-\-public-health
Keep
.B /health
unauthenticated when a token is required. Useful for load balancers
and uptime checks on non-loopback binds.
.TP
.B \-\-footgun
Disable all protections. Equivalent to
.B \-\-no-origin-check
and
.BR \-\-cors .
Intended for local development only.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-concurrent " n"
Maximum number of concurrent model requests. Default
.BR 5 .
Additional requests are queued.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DEV_SYSTEM_PROMPT
Default system prompt for every invocation.
.TP
.B DEV_MCP
Comma-separated list of MCP server paths or URLs to attach (a colon is
also accepted for local paths, but commas are canonical because a colon
would split remote URLs like
.BR https://host:8080 ).
Equivalent to repeating
.BR \-\-mcp .
.TP
.B DEV_MCP_TIMEOUT
MCP server timeout in seconds. Default
.BR 5 .
.TP
.B DEV_MCP_TOKEN
Bearer token for authenticating to remote MCP servers. Preferred
over
.B \-\-mcp-token
so the token does not appear in process lists.
.TP
.B DEV_HOST
Server bind address. Default
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.B DEV_PORT
Server port. Default
.BR 11434 .
.TP
.B DEV_TOKEN
Bearer token for server authentication. Equivalent to
.BR \-\-token .
.TP
.B DEV_TEMPERATURE
Default sampling temperature.
.TP
.B DEV_MAX_TOKENS
Default maximum number of tokens to generate.
.TP
.B DEV_CONTEXT_STRATEGY
Default context-management strategy.
.TP
.B DEV_CONTEXT_MAX_TURNS
Maximum history turns for the
.B sliding-window
strategy.
.TP
.B DEV_CONTEXT_OUTPUT_RESERVE
Tokens reserved for the model's output. Default
.BR 512 .
.TP
.B DEV_DEBUG
When set to any non-empty value, enables debug logging (same as
.BR \-\-debug ).
.TP
.B DEV_HISTFILE
Persist interactive
.B \-\-chat
line-editing history to this file across sessions. Off by default: when
unset (or empty), chat history is kept in memory only and nothing is
written to disk. When set, prior history is loaded at startup and the file
is rewritten (bounded to the most recent 500 entries, mode 0600) on exit.
A leading
.B ~
is expanded to the home directory.
.TP
.B DEV_TTS_VOICE
Default TTS voice identifier or
.B personal
for Personal Voice.
.TP
.B DEV_STT_LOCALE
Default speech recognition locale (e.g.
.BR en-US ).
.TP
.B DEV_TTS_RATE
Default speaking rate (0.25–4.0).
.TP
.B DEV_TTS_FORMAT
Default server TTS file format:
.BR wav ", "
.BR pcm ", or "
.BR aac .
.TP
.B DEV_AUDIO_INPUT
Default microphone device UID for
.BR \-\-listen " and "
.BR \-\-agent .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to any non-empty value, disables ANSI color output. See
.UR https://no-color.org
https://no-color.org
.UE .
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error, including tool execution errors and unexpected
failures.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error. Invalid flags, conflicting modes, or malformed values.
.TP
.B 3
Guardrail blocked. The input or output violated the active content
policy.
.TP
.B 4
Context overflow. The input exceeds the model's context window and
the active strategy was
.BR strict .
.TP
.B 5
Model unavailable. Apple Intelligence is not enabled or the on-device
model is not downloaded.
.TP
.B 6
Rate limited or busy. Exceeded
.BR \-\-max-concurrent ,
or a concurrent session lock is held.
.TP
.B 7
No code in response. With
.BR \-\-code ,
the model returned an empty response, so there is no code to print.
.TP
.B 8
Microphone permission denied. Grant Microphone access to the calling
terminal in System Settings.
.TP
.B 9
Speech recognition asset or engine failure.
.TP
.B 10
No suitable audio input device found.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted. The user pressed Ctrl-C (SIGINT) at the interactive chat
prompt. The terminal is restored to its normal mode before exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/dev
Binary installed by
.BR "make install" .
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/dev.1
This manual page.
.TP
.I $(brew --prefix)/bin/dev
Binary installed by
.BR "brew install dev" .
.TP
.I $(brew --prefix)/Cellar/dev/<version>/homebrew.mxcl.dev.plist
launchd plist used by the Homebrew service integration
.RB ( "brew services start dev" ).
.SH EXAMPLES
Send a single prompt:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
dev "What is the capital of Austria?"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Stream a haiku:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
dev --stream "Write a haiku about code"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run an interactive session with a custom personality:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
dev -s "You are a pirate" --chat
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pipe input from standard input:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
cat README.md | dev "Summarize this"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extract the response in JSON mode with
.BR jq (1):
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
dev -o json "Translate to German: hello" | jq -r .content
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start the OpenAI-compatible server on port 3000 with CORS:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
dev --serve --port 3000 --host 0.0.0.0 --cors
.fi
.RE
.PP
Attach an MCP calculator server and ask a math question:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
dev --mcp mcp/calculator/server.py "What is 127 * 31?"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Speak text aloud:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
dev --speak "Hello from SayItDev"
echo "Read this" | dev --speak
.fi
.RE
.PP
Transcribe from the default microphone:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
dev --listen
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run a voice Q&A agent (requires Apple Intelligence):
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
dev --agent
.fi
.RE
.PP
Synthesize speech over the HTTP API:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1/audio/speech \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{"input":"hello","voice":"default","response_format":"wav"}' \\
  --output hello.wav
.fi
.RE
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/innovatorved/sayitdev/issues
https://github.com/innovatorved/sayitdev/issues
.UE .
.PP
Known limitations:
.IP \[bu] 2
Context window is approximately 4096 tokens. Longer histories are
trimmed or rejected per the active context strategy.
.IP \[bu]
Embeddings, image generation, and image input are not supported;
the OpenAI-compatible server returns
.B 501 Not Implemented
for those endpoints.
.IP \[bu]
Requires Apple Silicon, macOS 26 (Tahoe) or newer, and Apple
Intelligence enabled in System Settings.
.IP \[bu]
On-device TTS supports
.BR wav ", "
.BR pcm ", and "
.BR aac
only; request
.B mp3
or
.B opus
over the HTTP API returns 400.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR jq (1),
.BR curl (1),
.BR brew (1),
.BR man (1).
.PP
Project homepage and full documentation:
.UR https://github.com/innovatorved/sayitdev
https://github.com/innovatorved/sayitdev
.UE .
